    "working_thesis": "Hannah Arendt's The Human Condition provides a phenomenological and historical analysis of the vita activa (labor, work, and action), challenging the traditional subordination of activity to contemplation, diagnosing the modern rise of society and alienation, and examining the loss and necessity of the public and private realms."
